  "verbalization": "Isoliquiritigenin is implicated in the regulation of Riboflavin synthase through a multi-step pathway involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferases. The evidence suggests that Isoliquiritigenin acts as a target for UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15 and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which in turn target Marlignan J, a compound that ultimately interacts with Riboflavin synthase. These findings indicate a potential mechanism by which Isoliquiritigenin may modulate Riboflavin synthase activity, possibly through the inhibition of UDP-glucuronosyltransferases, which are involved in the metabolism of various compounds, including riboflavin. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Isoliquiritigenin in influencing riboflavin biosynthesis, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a consistent relationship across different target entities, supporting the hypothesis that Isoliquiritigenin may exert its effects on Riboflavin synthase through a pathway involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferases.",
